      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cephalalgia, a common complaint, often presents both a diagnostic and a therapeutic problem. In a significant number of cases the cause may be traced to allergic sensitivity. \"Allergic headache\" is no different from other allergic diseases either as to the factors that produce the head pain or as to the specific treatment required. Taking a careful history and carrying out definitive skin testing may lead to diagnosis in cases that otherwise might be considered functional."},
